# =============================================================================
# Logs, temporary files, editor backups, crash dumps
# =============================================================================
*.log
*.log.*
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.backup
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
*.stackdump
# Core dumps only, anchored to the repository root. A bare `core` matches any
# file OR directory of that name at any depth, which silently swallowed the
# vendored JSON Schema vocabulary files
# (`_vendor/jsonschema_specifications/schemas/draft*/vocabularies/core`). The
# in-tree copies survived only because they were committed before this pattern
# existed — git ignores untracked files only — so the breakage surfaced only
# when a new tree carrying the same vendored payload was added.
/core
/core.[0-9]*

# =============================================================================
# Archives — listed as commented-out entries; uncomment to ignore individual
# extensions in projects that ship binary archive deliverables.
# =============================================================================
# *.zip
# *.tar
# *.tar.gz
# *.tgz
# *.7z
# *.rar
